{"format":"helia-content","version":1,"id":"comparison-functor","title":{"Inline":[{"Text":"The comparison functor of an adjunction"}]},"title_text":"The comparison functor of an adjunction","kind":"definition","taxon":null,"url":"comparison-functor.html","content":{"Block":[{"Group":{"role":"env","attrs":[["entry","comparison-functor"],["kind","definition"],["label","Definition"],["numbered","true"]],"body":{"Block":[{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"An adjunction "},{"Math":{"src":"F ⊣ U"}},{"Text":" with "},{"Math":{"src":"F : cal(C) -> cal(D)"}},{"Text":" and "},{"Math":{"src":"U : cal(D) -> cal(C)"}},{"Text":" induces a monad "},{"Math":{"src":"T = U ∘ F"}},{"Text":" on "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(C)"}},{"Text":". Write "},{"Math":{"src":"epsilon : F ∘ U => sans(\"Id\")"}},{"Text":" for the "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"counit"}]},{"Text":" of the adjunction. Every object "},{"Math":{"src":"d"}},{"Text":" of "},{"Math":{"src":"cal(D)"}},{"Text":" then induces a "},{"Math":{"src":"T"}},{"Text":"-algebra carried by the object "},{"Math":{"src":"U d"}},{"Text":", witnessed by the map"}]},{"Math":{"src":"U epsilon_d : U F U d -> U d ."}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"This assignment extends to a functor into the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"eilenberg-moore-displayed","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"Eilenberg–Moore category"}]}},{"Text":","}]},{"Math":{"src":"K : cal(D) -> \"EM\" lr(( T )) ,"}},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"the "},{"Emph":[{"Text":"comparison functor"}]},{"Text":" of the adjunction."}]},{"Paragraph":[{"Text":"Dually, an adjunction induces a comonad on the other side and a comparison into the "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"co-eilenberg-moore-displayed","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"co-Eilenberg–Moore category"}]}},{"Text":". When these comparisons are equivalences we say that the adjunction "},{"Math":{"src":"F ⊣ U"}},{"Text":" is "},{"EntryLink":{"id":"monadicity-comonadicity","label":null,"body":[{"Text":"(co)monadic"}]}},{"Text":"."}]}]}}}]}}
